==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|stinga}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*stinganą}}. Compare Faroese and Swedish {{m|fo|stinga}}, English {{m|en|sting}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈstiŋka/}}
* {{rhymes|is|iŋka|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|stakk|stungu|stungið}}

# to [[stab]], to [[sting]], to [[prick]] {{+obj|is|&intransitive/acc}}
# to [[wound]], to [[hurt]] {{+obj|is|&intransitive/acc}}
#: {{syn|is|særa}}
# to [[prick]] with something, to [[stab]] with something {{+obj|is|dat}}
#: {{ux|is|Hann '''stakk''' hnífnum í borðið.|He '''stuck''' the knife in the table.}}
# to [[slip]] something, to [[put]] something {{+obj|is|dat}}
#: {{ux|is|Prinsessan '''stakk''' einhverju í vasa bóndans.|The princess '''slipped''' something into the farmer's pocket.}}
#: {{ux|is|Hún hætti lestri og '''stakk''' skruddunni í hilluna.|She stopped reading and '''put''' the old book into the shelf.}}
# {{lb|is|impersonal}} to [[strike]] someone
#: {{ux|is|Það '''stakk''' mig.|It '''struck''' me.}}

